Krita Nova 46 - export brush presets as a bundle

The brush presets (the presets popup of the brush panel / toolbar, the Brush
Presets docker and the brush editor's preset list) get an "Export Brushes..."
button next to "Import Brushes...". It saves the presets the list
shows - the chosen category (and search) - as a Krita resource bundle
(.bundle):

- with everything they use: brush tips, patterns, gradients, ... (their
  linked resources, and what those use);
- the presets keep their category: the bundle tags them with it, so loading
  the bundle (Settings > Manage Resource Libraries > Import) brings the
  category back; "All" exports every preset;
- the bundle is named after the category, with a thumbnail made of the first
  nine presets;
- written to a temporary file and copied to the chosen place, which can be a
  content:// URI on Android.

Photoshop brush plugin: the "export_brush_presets" action and
KisPresetBundleExporter (KoResourceBundle). KisPresetChooser: Import and
Export side by side; the chooser whose button was pressed is passed to the
action.
